🚀 My First End-to-End CI/CD Pipeline Project! 🚀

I'm thrilled to share my latest project where I successfully built a complete CI/CD pipeline using Jenkins, GitHub, Maven, Docker, Amazon ECR, and Kubernetes. This pipeline automates the entire process of building, testing, and deploying a sample Java web application.

🧩 Problem Statement
Create an end-to-end CI/CD pipeline in AWS using Jenkins as the orchestration tool, GitHub as the SCM, Maven as the build tool, Docker for containerization, Amazon ECR for image storage, and Kubernetes (EKS) for deployment. The goal was to build and deploy a sample Java web app using Maven.

🏗️ Architecture Overview
Source Code Management: Java code stored in a GitHub repository.
Build: Jenkins uses Maven to build the Java application on a Tomcat server.
Dockerization: The application is packaged into a Docker image.
Image Storage: The Docker image is stored in Amazon ECR.
Deployment: The Docker image is deployed to a Kubernetes cluster (EKS).
