🔑 Key Steps
Source Code Management

Installed Git, generated SSH keys, and pushed the Java project to GitHub.
Build

Configured Jenkins with Maven and GitHub.
Built the project and deployed it on a Tomcat server.
Dockerization

Created a Docker image of the built project.
Pushed the image to Amazon ECR.
Deployment

Deployed the Docker image to a Kubernetes cluster using EKS.
🎯 Outcome
The entire process is now fully automated! Any code changes pushed to GitHub are automatically built, tested, and deployed—ensuring seamless updates to the live application. This project has been a fantastic learning experience in integrating multiple DevOps tools to create a robust and scalable CI/CD pipeline.

